  "isorophus_prior_checkpoint": "references/isorophus-inspection.json in raw evidence predates its concept",
  "source_reading": {
    "isorophus": "Bell1974 pp149-154 and textfig23B personally read/viewed before Isorophus concept, plus Ordovician Atlas OUIP I.cincinnatiensis actual fossil photograph. Four rays I-IV counterclockwise, V clockwise; low dome, alternating primary/secondary double biserial coverplates, narrow imbricate peripheral circlets, four main irregular oral plates with accessory orals. Fossil collapse not live holes.",
    "eleutherocrinus": "Whiteaves1889 p110, plate14 caption and figs5/5a/5b personally viewed: Goodwillie1882 Thedford specimen deposited in Museum of Geological Survey, four long ambulacra and single broad short one. Personally viewed actual Smithsonian photographs S4960 and S4963 (record metadata last modified8Sep2026, cited Millendorf1979). S4960 detailed side photo shows elongate theca and longitudinal plated ambulacral strips. S4963 fragment images not used to invent complete outline. Fay1961 primary indexed genus text p69 uses shortened D. Bohaty,Macurda,Waters2024 author-upload relevant text pp56-58 read; AB-to-D resting axis, four spiracles plus anispiracle, inferential C/E stouter brachioles. Use named D convention in this paper, not unverified A label. Stem absent; exact complete brachiole deployment uncertain.",
    "nucleocrinus": "Fay1961 primary indexed p84 and plate29 caption read in full relevant context: N.elegans topotype Chicago19049 is subglobular,8.5mm axial by11mm transverse; five arrow-like oral plates, paired side plates,10spiracles plus anal opening,3basals and a round crenellar stem. Fay separates Elaeacrinus/Placoblastus; old Ontario specimens labelled elegans may be meloniformis; Whiteaves1889 plate14fig2 not adopted as species identification. Sumrall etal2009 author-upload relevant discussion read: elongate Elaeacrinus/Placoblastus versus Nucleocrinus; N.bosei assignment tentative, not selected. Personally viewed current university Atlas N.elegans actual specimen photo with caption UMMP IP2041 (UMMP1949) and image alt1949; accession ambiguity recorded, no asserted type. It is more ovoid than Fay topotype, so museum pixels support longitudinal plated grooves, not chosen type proportions. No3D mesh downloaded. UMORF IP61801 metadata read but model not loaded. Chosen same-genus species N.elegans with type-text subglobular reconstruction, not uncritical elongated old reconstruction. Full Fay PDF download failed; HTML responses preserved, no claim full original plate viewed.",
    "placocystites": "Ruta1998 full scanned paper pp173-182 consulted, normal textfig1A-D personally viewed, abnormal HC11 photos explicitly excluded from normal plating. Normal fossil photos BIRUG18327 in Hickman2010 BCGS200p15 and named Dudley specimen in Groves2010 BCGS201p14 personally viewed. Body flattened rounded rectangle with slight asymmetry, dorsal and ventral large irregular plates, ventral three-anterior-plate condition, two oral marginal spines and one aulacophore. Normal lower plates and slender oral spines visible in Dudley photo. Aulacophore has broad proximal, tapering middle and fine distal part; complete distal extension inferred from primary normal figure. Historical chordate gills/head/tail interpretations excluded; geometry only observable plates/spines/articulated appendage, no asserted function.",
    "general_blastoid_caveat": "2024 Waters et al Feeding postures as indicators of mutable collagenous tissue in extinct echinoderms DOI10.1038/s42003-024-07232-z primary text consulted: articulated brachioles are rare, stem morphology/posture may not be generalized to an exact genus; our complete Nucleocrinus stem and brachiole deployment are explicit low-confidence reconstructive choices, not claims measured from pictured isolated theca."
  },
